gm-method (exact terrain collider baked from live GPU shader tiles): bake height patches from the real GPU shader via globalThis.__thcBakeReadback into physics - whole-planet, exact composeHeight, nothing stored; ~2ms/130^2 tile, ~200-400x faster than CPU fractal AND faster than a JS lookup. Tile->world convention must be pinned gap 0.00/texel. Patch density tracks the FINEST display LOD = 2R/2^maxLevel/(gridMeshSize-1), and the physics grid resolution is clamped to it so collider == drawn surface. The three files: PatchBaker.js, TerrainPhysics.createGpuPatchHeightFn.